notes:
From the coverage analysis (2026-11-18): 19 hand-written calls are shortcuts (the author wrote A -> C, the code goes A -> B -> C). Tidy should not call them repeated; it can offer the exact path instead, or keep them as the author's summary. See docair-4wk.17 for how --coverage counts them.
CLI and server side (this session): crates/docair-core/src/tidy.rs repeated(graph) and changes(): an authored line tag (calls, in/out with from/to, reads, writes, emits, consumes, creates, routes, selects) is repeated when the same part has an inferred tag of the same name to the same target with no reach (certain), and the tag has no words and no wording of what travels that differs from the code's; shortcuts and @covers never. Test only_a_certain_wordless_tag_the_code_says_is_repeated. crates/docair-cli/src/tidy.rs: docair tidy [root] [--out] [--apply] lists them by file with the code's place, writes docair.patch, --apply writes and scans again; docair build and check end with 'n tags repeat the code: run docair tidy'. docair-server: GET /api/tidy {tags, patch}, POST /api/tidy {tags?} -> ServeApplied (409 when none), at / for docair serve and under /api/projects/<id>/; test tidy_lists_and_removes_the_tags_the_code_repeats; openapi.yaml. Run on docair: 4 found (main.rs @calls cmd_word, discover/env/extract @in … from), applied, 0 left; docair check 0/0. SPEC CLI table and §10.5 routes, ADAPTERS §6.1, meanings.toml (repeated tag, served project). UI (header button, banner, panel, Tags tab, copy command, download patch): the other session.
Page side (docair-viewer). The new page_tidy.rs takes docair_core::tidy::repeated(graph) and builds:
- the header's '✂ Tidy · n' (accent) or '✂ Tidy ✓', next to the diagnostics;
- a banner as a grid row under the header ('n tags repeat what the code says. Review and tidy'), closed for the reader until the count changes (localStorage docair:tidy:<system>);
- the panel (P.tidy), by the block's file and then by block, each tag ticked with 'the code says <tag> · file:line (reason)', plus Copy command (docair tidy --apply);
- Apply ('✂ Tidy the ticked tags') and ⤓ Patch, which show once a server answers (body[data-served], set when /api/ai answers);
- in each part's Tags tab, a mark '✂ the code says this · file:line' with 'Tidy this tag', served only.
page.js: Apply and Tidy this tag POST the ticked tags, or one, to /api/tidy and reload; opening the panel fetches GET /api/tidy and shows the patch; ⤓ Patch downloads it. Room was made in wireChat (say() and download() helpers), so page.js is at 998 of 1,000 lines. The Tags tab now uses docair_core::check::KNOWN_TAGS, so @covers, @carried-as and @path no longer show as unknown. docs/meanings.toml settles [tidy]. Tests: tests/page.rs the_page_offers_to_tidy_the_tags_the_code_repeats; e2e/fixtures/tidy (one @calls the code makes, excluded from docair's own scan) and e2e/tests/tidy.spec.ts ('a page opened as a file counts them and offers the command'; 'docair serve tidies the ticked tags, and then nothing repeats'). SPEC §3.5, ADAPTERS §6.1.

description:
Warnings when description and code disagree (codes picked after docair-4wk.6):

- an operation that no code in its service serves, when the service has code (never for external parts);
- a route served in a described service that its description lacks; [[import.api]] ignore silences single routes;
- an operationId that names a function in the service whose route differs: W103 stale (ADAPTERS.md §6: the code wins);
- a hint when the operations are served in another service: "set part_of".

API descriptions (OpenAPI, AsyncAPI) declare rendezvous points with their types: the HTTP routes a service offers, the topics it sends and receives. docair reads them as one more adapter that produces facts (ADAPTERS.md §4); the core matches them with what the code serves and requests (§7). Then:

- a handler gets its operation's text and types;
- a caller's line gets what it sends and gets back, with the description as evidence;
- an operation nobody implements shows as an endpoint;
- description and code that disagree warn.

Builds on the adapters epic docair-4wk: the facts model (docair-4wk.2) and cross-language HTTP matching (docair-4wk.6). Exports (Mermaid, LikeC4, Backstage, Structurizr) are left out for now.

design:
Fixture e2e/fixtures/apis:
- api/Cargo.toml declares orders-api (placement by directory);
- api/src/lib.rs: create_order POST /api/orders; get_order GET /api/orders/{orderId} (the description says {id}); update_order PUT /api/order/{id} (stale route, Import 3); list_orders GET /api/orders (undescribed, Import 3);
- api/openapi.yaml: 3.1, servers [{url: /api}], createOrder, getOrder, update_order, cancelOrder (no handler);
- ui/src/cart.ts: a request for POST /api/orders without payload words, and one for POST /v1/charges;
- vendor/payments-openapi.json: title Payments, several operations, one called; docs/payments.md declares payments as external.
